  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-04T08:50:47.786Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please disable screen space ambient occlusion in both the client and SDK for the post processing stack v1.\n\nAmbient occlusion provided in the v1 post processing stack reduces the screen resolution, noticeably degrading clarity in VR to the point of eye strain. World creators who do not have VR headsets often do not know this, on top of downsampling being enabled by default which makes it even worse. Some very cool and creative worlds are utterly ruined by how harsh they are on the eyes because of this.\n\nAdditional warnings in the SDK against using effects unsuitable for VR would also be helpful, and maybe also pushing creators to move to post processing stack v2. Ambient occlusion in post processing stack v2 is still unpleasant in VR but does not seem to suffer the same resolution problems.",
